                         GUIDE: NETWORK AND SSH
      (arrows/PgUp/PgDn to scroll, / to search, q to quit; "help" lists
                             all commands)

No network is needed to install: everything is on the ISO. It is only
needed to cast spells that aren't on it (other boot loaders, systemd) or to
install from another computer.

1. GETTING ONLINE
-----------------
@[ip link] lists the network interfaces (e.g. enp1s0 wired, wlan0 or
wlp0s20f3 Wi-Fi); replace wlan0 below with yours.

  wired:  @[dhcpcd]
  Wi-Fi:  @[wpa_passphrase 'NETWORK' 'PASSWORD' > /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf]
          @[wpa_supplicant -B -i wlan0 -c /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf]
          @[dhcpcd wlan0]

Check with @[ping -c 3 kernel.org]. The installed system has the same tools
(copy /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf to $ENCHANT_TARGET/etc/ to keep the Wi-Fi
setting).


2. INSTALLING OVER SSH
----------------------
To install from another computer, run these three commands here:
  @[passwd]                                  (set a root password)
  @[ssh-keygen -A]                           (create the host keys)
  @[/usr/sbin/sshd -o PermitRootLogin=yes]   (start the SSH server)
then on the other computer: @[ssh root@ADDRESS] (@[ip addr] shows this
machine's address).

The host keys are new at every boot of the ISO, so after a reboot ssh warns
"REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED". That is expected here: forget the
old key on the other computer with @[ssh-keygen -R ADDRESS] and connect
again.
